			"Message": "fix(Sky): Fix URI object construction for workbench search result deduplication\n\nThe previous manual resource object construction (`{ $mid: 1, path, scheme }`) fails when the workbench attempts result deduplication via `uri.with({...})` because it's a POJO without methods, causing \"uri.with is not a function\" errors.\n\nThis commit adds `CelUriCtor` and `CelUri` interfaces to type VS Code's URI class, then creates `MakeFileUri` that uses the actual `Ctor.file()` method when `__CEL_SERVICES__.URI` is available. The lookup is re-resolved on each result construction to handle the event-rescue path where SkyBridge registers before the URI patch binds.\n\nUpdates both `MatchFromHit` (text search results) and file search result mapping to use `MakeFileUri` instead of manual object construction. Includes a last-resort POJO fallback for edge cases.\n\nAlso updates Output submodule to expose the URI class from vscode-uri to the workbench accessor exports, providing the full prototype chain (`.with()`, `.fsPath`, `.toString()`) needed by SkyBridge's search provider.\n\nImpact: Search results now properly deduplicate in the workbench, eliminating duplicate file entries in quick open and search views.",
			"SHA": "c32ec836f94f03bf6fcaf88edd6a837e5c06fd9a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T09:00:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Cocoon, Output, Sky, Wind, and Worker submodules\n\nRoutine submodule synchronization bringing in latest changes across the application stack:\n\n1. Sky (70de1fdb):\n   - Extract worker script imports into dedicated WorkerBundleImports.astro component to fix Astro compiler hoisting issue in JSX conditionals\n   - Add comprehensive RenderDevLog diagnostics for search operations\n   - Replace single-shot workbench-ready retry with three parallel rescue paths for search provider registration\n   - Add SearchRegistered flag to prevent duplicate registration attempts\n\n2. Worker (e8bdbb87):\n   - Expand minified ESBuild config files with source maps\n   - Reverse minification (cc40eef) to aid debugging ESBuild pipeline issues while preserving configuration logic\n\n3. Cocoon (ca5878fa), Output (6b389ee0), Wind (56a0603f):\n   - Submodule sync to latest changes\n\nThe Sky refactor resolves bundle-mode build failures where Astro's script processing couldn't handle conditional rendering, while improving search functionality resilience.",
			"SHA": "99a19decd5ce52a75b94ffb1186c8b8fe358d4b9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-25T02:04:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				3
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Cocoon, Output, and Sky submodules\n\nRoutine submodule synchronization bringing in latest changes across the application stack:\n\n1. Output (36ce8f4a):\n- Expand CopyVSRootFiles candidate resolution to check both `<root>/<file>` and `<root>/vs/<file>` paths since nls.* files and other VS Code outputs exist at different locations depending on TSC pass\n- Add NODE_ENV-aware ordering: production prioritizes `out-build/` (release TSC flat layout) before `out/` (debug TSC source layout), development does the reverse\n- Preserve tier 4 inline stub fallback for missing NLS files\n\n2. Sky (87d32133):\n- Restore Bundle mode distinction for worker script loading in Electron.astro\n- Bundle=true profiles use npm-package imports inside single <script> block for Vite bundling\n- Bundle=false profiles continue using separate <script> tags for static assets\n- Maintain CSS Load → Policy → Register ordering requirement\n\n3. Cocoon (8715468b):\n- Submodule sync to latest extension host changes\n\nImpact: Output now correctly copies NLS files from both root and vs/ directories. Sky restores compatibility with both bundled and non-bundled build profiles. Extension host updated to latest.",
			"SHA": "f92044ca8c1bb62925624a012bba8d29f9757cd3"
